    {
        "id": "ja:word:social-gratitude",
        "label": "ありがとうございます",
        "class": "lexical:interjection",
        "fields": {
            "pronunciation": ["ありがとうございます"],
            "usage_notes": {
                "en": "Polite thanks, suitable for a teacher or someone outside a close relationship. ありがとう alone is more familiar. Preserve the long とう sound. The helpful scene supports gratitude but cannot determine exact wording.",
                "de": "Höflicher Dank, passend gegenüber Lehrkräften oder weniger vertrauten Personen. ありがとう allein ist vertrauter. Den langen とう-Laut bewahren. Die Hilfsszene stützt Dankbarkeit, legt den Wortlaut aber nicht fest.",
                "id": "Ucapan terima kasih sopan, sesuai untuk guru atau orang yang tidak akrab. ありがとう saja lebih akrab. Pertahankan bunyi panjang とう. Adegan bantuan mendukung rasa terima kasih, bukan kata-kata tertentu.",
                "ja": "先生や親しくない相手にも使える丁寧な感謝。ありがとうだけならより親しい調子。とうの長音を保つ。手助けの場面は感謝を補うが、正確な発話は特定しない。"
            },
            "reference_images": [
                "images/2e41c9a5ddddd56803d890f628a1761eeb14aa7a40b9406fd1f336196af00e49.jpg"
            ],
            "audio": "audio/c9b899d628475551a35326efd0cd9f464fed35f97692c7caeaf8c4345e593583.wav"
        },
